## 1. Overview & Objectives
Store Management REST API for the EEI6369 AWS Cloud Computing practical assessment. Deployed on
AWS EC2 with Docker, database on Amazon RDS PostgreSQL. No frontend. See `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md`.

- Working, production-style Spring Boot API: products, categories, inventory
- Secure, env-var-based configuration; Docker image; GitHub Actions DevSecOps pipeline
- Easy deployment to EC2 + RDS

## 2. Requirements & Features
| ID | Requirement / feature | Priority | Status | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| R1 | Product CRUD `/api/products` (name req., price > 0, qty >= 0, unique SKU, timestamps) | High | Done | SKU trimmed + upper-cased |
| R2 | Search products by name, filter by category | High | Done | `GET /api/products?name=&category=` (case-insensitive) |
| R3 | Check available stock | High | Done | `GET /api/products/{id}/stock?required=N` |
| R4 | Category CRUD `/api/categories` (unique name) | High | Done | Product.category stays a free-text String (per spec) |
| R5 | Inventory increase/decrease, no negative stock, error on insufficient | High | Done | `POST /api/products/{id}/stock/{increase,decrease}`, 409 |
| R6 | Layered architecture, constructor DI, DTOs, `@RestControllerAdvice`, Jakarta validation | High | Done | |
| R7 | PostgreSQL via env vars DB_HOST/PORT/NAME/USERNAME/PASSWORD; validate schema in prod; local profile | High | Done | Flyway + `ddl-auto: validate`; `application-local.yml` |
| R8 | Actuator `/actuator/health` (db UP) + `/actuator/info`, no sensitive info | High | Done | show-components always, show-details never |
| R9 | Multi-stage Dockerfile, non-root, port 8080, healthcheck; `.dockerignore`; docker-compose w/ volume | High | Done (not run locally) | Docker daemon not running on this PC |
| R10 | Tests: service, controller, repository, integration (JUnit 5 + Mockito) | High | Done | 63 tests pass |
| R11 | Springdoc OpenAPI, Swagger UI `/swagger-ui/index.html` | High | Done | |
| R12 | README with all required sections | High | Done | |
| R13 | GitHub Actions `devsecops.yml` | High | Done (not run yet) | needs GitHub remote |

## 3. Technology Stack & Architecture
- **Languages / frameworks:** Java 17, Spring Boot 3.3.5 (Web, Data JPA, Validation, Actuator), springdoc-openapi 2.6.0
- **Runtime / platform:** Docker (eclipse-temurin:17-jre-alpine) on AWS EC2
- **Data storage:** PostgreSQL 16 (Amazon RDS in prod; docker-compose locally; H2 PostgreSQL-mode in tests)
- **Key libraries / services:** Flyway (schema), Hikari, JUnit 5, Mockito, MockMvc; GitHub Actions, Gitleaks, Trivy, GHCR
- **Architecture summary:** Controller → Service (@Transactional) → Repository (Spring Data JPA, Specifications, pessimistic lock for stock) → PostgreSQL. DTO records separate from entities. GlobalExceptionHandler returns `ApiErrorResponse` JSON.
- **How to run:** `docker compose up --build -d` (after `cp .env.example .env`), or `./mvnw spring-boot:run` with DB env vars + `SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=local`
- **How to test:** `./mvnw verify` (no Docker needed)
- **How to build / deploy:** `docker build -t store-management-api .`; on EC2 `docker run` with RDS env vars (see README "AWS deployment considerations")

